    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-21T21:36:47+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-21T21:36:47+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T11:06:47Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T11:06:47Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure lingers north of the border over the Northern Territory. A slow moving high pressure system in the Tasman Sea maintains a ridge across eastern parts of the state. A trough of low pressure is forecast to move into the west on Thursday, and slowly move eastwards on Friday. Another trough and multiple cold fronts move over the state over the weekend.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW007" description="Murraylands" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-21T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Light winds.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">The chance of fog in the early morning. Mostly sunny day. Light winds becoming north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the early morning then becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">No Rating</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers from the late morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h shifting south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late morning and early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 17 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds southerly and light increasing to 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching 23 to 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching around 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
